  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "Y0BhbJ7X6Gr0fPmmYRGevHh3mUw=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:05.355Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "JN Data is a jointly owned operations and hosting utility, not a builder. That is a disqualifier rather than a low score: the firm's mandate is to run systems on behalf of its owners, so there is no development practice for a partnership to attach to.\n\nThe distinction is worth keeping sharp, because a shared Nordic IT utility looks superficially like the bank-owned cooperatives elsewhere in this set. The cooperatives at least build; an operations utility consumes what others build. No open-source screen will change that, which makes this note a closing judgement rather than a research gap.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**4 \u00b7 needs OSS screen**\n- JN Data (DK)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Jointly owned operations and hosting utility, not a builder.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:30:05.355832Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:05.355837Z"
    }
  },
